{
  "name": "Canonical Wire Byte Length V1",
  "description": "Measure the UTF-8 byte length of Language canonicalText for the opened exact root. Preserve nested native references; do not serialize the transitive evidence graph. The input is exactly one input operand. Reject unavailable root content and invalid Unicode. Charge 5 base units, then ordinary logical native value construction/validation charges. Before canonicalization, reserve closure work in deterministic depth-first field order: 1 per manifest attempt; 8 times field count times one plus ceil(log2(field count)) for members; 8 per list item; 8 per started 64 units of six times each UTF-16 text/key length (keys also multiplied by sort rounds plus one); 8 times squared magnitude-based 32-bit Integer limbs. For native Integer decimal String payloads reserve ceil(4 times decimal digits / 32) limbs before conversion, excluding a minus sign; inspect exact type ancestry with 1 per edge, reference text blocks and manifest charges. Reference identities cost 8 per started 64 UTF-16 units; follow each non-core reference once. Reservations cover canonical traversal, sorting, wire encoding, round-trip parsing/identity and UTF-8 encoding. No post-work gas charge. No application size limit or business decision belongs to this capability. The non-additive runtime marker and explicit binding select V1; previous bindings do not install it."
}
